<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH CBANK FOREX RESERVES DIP TO $12.4BLN END-DEC.</title>
<headline>CZECH CBANK FOREX RESERVES DIP TO $12.4BLN END-DEC.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign reserves at the Czech National Bank (CNB), the country's central bank, eased to $12.4 billion crowns at the end of December from $12.6 billion at the end of November, the CNB said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It added in a statement that forex reserves for the banking sector alone rose to $3.637 billion at the end of December from $3.25 at end-November.  </p>
<p> CZECH FOREIGN RESERVES	Dec 1996    Nov 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p>  Czech National Bank ($bln)  12.435	12.604	 14.02</p>
<p>  Commercial banks		 3.637	 3.250	  2.94</p>
<p>  total			     16.072	15.854	 16.96</p>
<p>Note. Measures through end of period. All 1996 figures</p>
<p>subject to revision.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2423-0003</p>
</text>
